-- policy.l4 — Codex Insurance Limited hospital-income policy, encoded in L4.
--
-- The DECLAREs and supporting helpers below this line, up to "Coverage decision",
-- are copied verbatim from inputs/schema.md so that this file is self-contained.
-- No claim data appears in this file.

IMPORT prelude

DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF Sickness, `Accidental injury`, Neither

DECLARE Cause IS ONE OF
  Skydiving, `Military service`, Firefighting, `Police service`, Other

DECLARE Claim
  HAS `agreement signed`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `premium paid month`                         IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `hospitalization month`                      IS A NUMBER
      `hospitalization ground`                     IS A Ground
      `age at hospitalization`                     IS A NUMBER
      `causes`                                     IS A LIST OF Cause
      `fraud month`                                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `misrepresentation month`                    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit month`                       IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `written confirmation month`                 IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `dispute arisen`                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `unable to settle month`                     IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `arbitration commenced month`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `valid arbitration award issued`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `written proof of claim month`               IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `recovery sought month`                      IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `policy term months`                         IS A NUMBER
      `confined in us hospital`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `continuous confinement days`                IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `claim made setting out basis`               IS A BOOLEAN

-- Supporting helpers (pre-defined — used as-is, not redefined)

GIVEN  `event month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
       `limit month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no later than` MEANS
  CONSIDER `event month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m AT MOST `limit month`

GIVEN  cs IS A LIST OF Cause
       c  IS A Cause
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arose out of` MEANS elem c cs

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Additional helper used by `covered` but not given by the schema: a presence
-- test for a MAYBE NUMBER field, used for events (fraud, misrepresentation,
-- premium payment) where what matters is only whether they happened at all,
-- not any deadline.

GIVEN  `occurrence month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`has occurred` MEANS
  CONSIDER `occurrence month`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST m  THEN TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§ `Section 1 — Policy in Effect and Conditions`

§§ `1.3 — the wellness-visit / confirmation condition`

-- "you will supply us with written confirmation ... of a wellness visit ...
-- occurring no later than the 6th month anniversary ..., no later than the
-- 7th month anniversary."  Both deadlines must be met, and the visit must
-- have been with a qualified medical provider, for the condition to be
-- satisfied outright.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the 1.3 condition is satisfied` claim MEANS
       `no later than` (claim's `wellness visit month`) 6
   AND claim's `wellness visit provider qualified`
   AND `no later than` (claim's `written confirmation month`) 7

-- 1.1(3): "The condition set out in Section 1.3 is still pending or has been
-- satisfied in a timely fashion."  Read against 1.1's own framing ("in effect
-- ... at the time of hospitalization"), "still pending" means the ultimate
-- 7-month deadline for the condition has not yet passed as of the
-- hospitalization.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the 1.3 condition is still pending` claim MEANS
    claim's `hospitalization month` LESS THAN 7

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the 1.3 condition holds` claim MEANS
       `the 1.3 condition is satisfied` claim
   OR  `the 1.3 condition is still pending` claim

§§ `1.2 — Cancelation`

-- "Cancelation will be deemed to have occurred if there is fraud, or any
-- misrepresentation or material withholding of any information ..., or if
-- the condition set out in Section 1.3 has not been satisfied in a timely
-- fashion.  It will also be automatically canceled ... on the last day of
-- the policy term."

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the policy has expired by its term` claim MEANS
    claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN claim's `policy term months`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the policy has been canceled` claim MEANS
       `has occurred` (claim's `fraud month`)
   OR  `has occurred` (claim's `misrepresentation month`)
   OR  NOT (`the 1.3 condition holds` claim)
   OR  `the policy has expired by its term` claim

§§ `1.1 — Policy in effect`

-- "The policy will be in effect if: 1. This agreement is signed, 2. The
-- applicable premium ... has been paid, and 3. The condition set out in
-- Section 1.3 is still pending or has been satisfied ..., and 4. The policy
-- has not been canceled."

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the policy is in effect` claim MEANS
       claim's `agreement signed`
   AND `has occurred` (claim's `premium paid month`)
   AND `the 1.3 condition holds` claim
   AND NOT (`the policy has been canceled` claim)

§ `Section 2 — Benefits`

-- 2.1: "If you have been confined in a hospital as a result of sickness or
-- accidental Injury, we will pay you the Daily Hospital Income Benefit."
-- `Neither` is neither sickness nor accidental injury, so it is not a
-- covered ground (e.g. a deliberate, non-accidental act).

GIVEN g IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a covered ground` g MEANS
    CONSIDER g
      WHEN Sickness            THEN TRUE
      WHEN `Accidental injury` THEN TRUE
      WHEN Neither             THEN FALSE

-- 2.2: the benefit is payable only "for each (24 hour) day of continuous
-- confinement in a hospital in the United States."  Whether that confinement
-- runs past the 365-day cap bears only on how much is paid, not on whether
-- any benefit is payable at all, so `covered` does not test the cap.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the confinement qualifies for a benefit` claim MEANS
       claim's `confined in us hospital`
   AND `has occurred` (claim's `continuous confinement days`)

§ `Section 3 — General Exclusions`

-- 3.1: no benefit for sickness or accidental injury "arising directly or
-- indirectly out of" skydiving, military service, firefighting, or police
-- service, or where the claimant's age at hospitalization is 80 or above.

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an excluded cause is present` claim MEANS
       `arose out of` (claim's causes) Skydiving
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's causes) `Military service`
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's causes) Firefighting
   OR  `arose out of` (claim's causes) `Police service`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the claimant is excluded by age` claim MEANS
    claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a general exclusion applies` claim MEANS
       `an excluded cause is present` claim
   OR  `the claimant is excluded by age` claim

§ `Section 4.2 — Arbitration`

-- "such arbitration to be commenced within three (3) months from the day
-- such parties are unable to settle the dispute ... If You fail to commence
-- arbitration in accordance with this clause, ... any cause of action and
-- any right to make a claim ... shall be extinguished completely.  Where
-- there is a dispute ..., the issuance of a valid arbitration award shall
-- also be a condition precedent to our liability."

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arbitration was commenced in time` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `unable to settle month`
      WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
      WHEN JUST m  THEN `no later than` (claim's `arbitration commenced month`) (m PLUS 3)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the arbitration condition is satisfied` claim MEANS
       NOT (claim's `dispute arisen`)
   OR  (   `arbitration was commenced in time` claim
       AND claim's `valid arbitration award issued`)

-- "In no case shall You seek to recover on this Policy before the expiration
-- of sixty (60) days after written proof of claim has been submitted to Us."
-- Sixty days is two of this policy's months (60 / 30), consistent with the
-- month-denominated deadlines used everywhere else in this schema.

GIVEN  claim IS A Claim
       r     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`recovery was not sought too soon after proof` claim r MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `written proof of claim month`
      WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
      WHEN JUST w  THEN r AT LEAST (w PLUS 2)

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the recovery timing condition is satisfied` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `recovery sought month`
      WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
      WHEN JUST r  THEN `recovery was not sought too soon after proof` claim r

§ `Coverage decision`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
covered claim MEANS
       `the policy is in effect` claim
   AND `is a covered ground` (claim's `hospitalization ground`)
   AND `the confinement qualifies for a benefit` claim
   AND claim's `claim made setting out basis`
   AND NOT (`a general exclusion applies` claim)
   AND `the arbitration condition is satisfied` claim
   AND `the recovery timing condition is satisfied` claim
